[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 500,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 539,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69759,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 103,
        "headingId": 539,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cowper gland adenocarcinoma is a tumour of the periurethral bulbomembranous glands, with features of adenoid cystic carcinoma of the salivary glands.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:12:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 501,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 540,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69760,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 103,
        "headingId": 540,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8140/3 Carcinoma of Cowper glands</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:12:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 502,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 541,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69761,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 103,
        "headingId": 541,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2C93.0 &amp; XH22Z8 Adenocarcinoma of urethra or paraurethral gland &amp; Carcinoma of Skene, Cowper, and Littr&eacute; glands</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:12:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 503,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 542,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69762,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 103,
        "headingId": 542,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> urethral accessory gland adenocarcinoma; adenoid cystic carcinoma of the Cowper gland.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:12:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 504,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 543,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69763,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 103,
        "headingId": 543,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:12:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 505,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 544,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69764,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 103,
        "headingId": 544,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cowper gland adenocarcinoma is localized in the bulbomembranous urethra with infiltrative growth to surrounding tissues {27554206}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:12:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 506,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 545,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69765,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 103,
        "headingId": 545,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cowper gland adenocarcinoma usually manifests as perianal or perirectal pain/discomfort, and/or urinary retention. Physical examination usually shows a hard, fixed mass in the infraprostatic area {4329938; 1311394; 27554206; 19127687; 24575017}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:12:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 507,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 546,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69766,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 103,
        "headingId": 546,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cowper gland adenocarcinoma is an extremely rare tumour. It affects men in the fifth to seventh decades of life {4329938; 1311394; 27554206; 19127687; 24575017}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:12:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 508,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 547,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69767,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 103,
        "headingId": 547,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:12:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 509,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 548,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69768,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 103,
        "headingId": 548,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The presence of <em>MYB</em>::<em>NFIB</em> fusion, which has been described in adenoid cystic carcinoma of the salivary glands and breast, has also been reported in Cowper gland adenocarcinoma of the urethra {24575017}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:12:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 516,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 555,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69769,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 103,
        "headingId": 555,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours are firm, lobulated, whitish-tan to yellow masses {27554206}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:12:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 510,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 549,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69770,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 103,
        "headingId": 549,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours have cribriform, trabecular, and solid patterns. Neoplastic cells have a bland appearance, with dark nuclei forming gland-like structures and rarely true tubules. Glandular/gland-like structures often contain mucoid material. Perineural spread is frequent. Immunohistochemistry for CK7 and high-molecular-weight cytokeratin is positive. Prostatic markers (PSA, PAP), CEA, S100, and SMA are negative {19127687; 27554206}.</p>\r\n<p>The diagnosis of a tumour arising from accessory paraurethral glands of the bulbomembranous urethra is challenging because most patients present with an advanced-stage tumour that frequently destroys the glandular tissues.</p>\r\n<p>The differential diagnosis includes urothelial carcinoma with extensive glandular differentiation, prostatic ductal adenocarcinoma, and basal cell carcinoma of the prostate.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:12:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 511,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 550,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69771,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 103,
        "headingId": 550,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:12:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 512,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 551,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69772,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 103,
        "headingId": 551,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:12:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 515,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 554,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69773,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 103,
        "headingId": 554,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a tumour with adenoid cystic carcinoma morphology; the tumour&rsquo;s relationship to the Cowper glands should be confirmed by clinical and radiological correlation; negativity for prostatic immunohistochemical markers.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> confirmation of <em>MYB</em>::<em>NFIB</em> fusion.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:12:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 513,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 552,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69774,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 103,
        "headingId": 552,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The eighth-edition American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) and Union for International Cancer Control (UICC) TNM system can be applied.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:12:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 514,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 553,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69775,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 103,
        "headingId": 553,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most patients present at an advanced stage and need additional treatment after surgery. Metastatic spread has been documented in the lung in one case and in the liver in another case {19127687; 24575017}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T19:12:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]